ctor of philosophy)"}],"ocaid":"hindubuddhistide0000unse","publish_places":["Surrey"],"isbn_13":["9781409443544","9781409443551"],"pagination":"pages cm.","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v39.i51.records.utf8:22155820:1318","marc:marc_marygrove/marygrovecollegelibrary.full.D20191108.T213022.internetarchive2nd_REPACK.mrc:192394076:5397","ia:hindubuddhistide0000unse","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:90099275:5339","bwb:9781409443544","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part38.utf8:223358133:1536","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:90152027:5339","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-032.mrc:86372569:3383","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:354555141:1616","amazon:140944354X","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_025.bib.mrc:178354068:4676"],"title":"Hindu and Buddhist ideas in dialogue","lccn":["2011050503"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/422"],"subjects":["Buddhism","Buddhist philosophy","Hinduism","Ātman","Hindu philosophy","Relations","Anātman"],"publish_date":"2012","publish_country":"enk","by_statement":"Edited by Irina Kuznetsova, Jonardon Ganeri and Chakravarthi Ram-Prasad","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16362267W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["952933828","768480356"],"number_of_pages":272,"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"The debates between various Buddhist and Hindu philosophical systems about the existence, definition and nature of self, occupy a central place in the history of Indian philosophy and religion. These debates concern various issues: what 'self' means, whether the self can be said to exist at all, arguments that can substantiate any position on this question, how the ordinary reality of individual persons can be explained, and the consequences of each position. At a time when comparable issues are at the forefront of contemporary Western philosophy, in both analytic and continental traditions (as well as in their interaction), these classical and medieval Indian debates widen and globalise such discussions. This book brings to a wider audience the sophisticated range of positions held by various systems of thought in classical India.\"--Publisher's website."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-12-28T11:32:42.470750"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-23T22:33:47.544986"}}},"ISBN:9782916915449":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9782916915449","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL24415980M/The_root_stanzas_on_the_Middle_Way","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL24415980M/The_root_stanzas_on_the_Middle_Way","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6667493-S.jpg","details":{"other_titles":["Mūlamadhyamakakārikā"],"publishers":["Edition Padmakara"],"translated_from":[{"key":"/languages/tib"}],"number_of_pages":200,"subtitle":"Mulamadhyamakakarika","contributors":[{"role":"Translator","name":"Padmakara Translation Group"}],"covers":[6667493],"physical_format":"Paperback","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-04-28T11:09:58.855321"},"latest_revision":6,"key":"/books/OL24415980M","publish_places":["Plazac, France"],"classifications":{},"title":"The root stanzas on the Middle Way","translation_of":"dbus ma rtsa ba shes rab 'phags pa klu sgrub kyis mdzad pa","notes":"A translation of Nagarjuna's famous work by the Padmakara Translation Group which was made to mark the visit of the Dalai Lama to France in August 2008 and as a support for the teachings given on that occasion. This is a translation of the Tibetan version of the original Sanskrit, following the commentary of the great Nyingma and Rimey master Mipham Rinpoche. This volume includes just the translation with the Tibetan text at the back.","identifiers":{},"created":{"type":"/type/dateti